  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation is on an explicit function with a body, `GraphWithChangingEdges`'s `Graph::node_content` in `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets`. That is a permitted target. The commentary is fenced and gives a substantive reason, not just difficulty. The reason matches the current source:\n- `node_content` is a required method of the trait (`crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs#trait[Graph]/fn[node_content]`), so the test has to define it.\n- The body is `panic!`, so any call would fail the test.\n- The test asserts that the only recorded dependency is `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`, so no content read is expected.\n- The agent script only calls `outgoing_edges` and then `submit_result`, so the function is never reached and has zero recorded execution.\n\nThe exception applies to this function only and does not excuse the file's threshold. No gap.",
